--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI TemperatureImpactPage at web parity: a pure @Observable state holder
(ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable TemperatureImpactDataSource seam whose method
names mirror the web hooks at the Swift call sites (loadVehicles ← useSelectedVehicle/GET /vehicles;
useTemperatureImpact ← the ['temperature-impact', vehicleId] query / GET
/analytics/temperature-impact?vehicle_id). Every web useMemo derivation is ported (avgEff = mean,
bucketAvgs over the five fixed °C bands, best = min-avg band, worst = max-avg band, total = points,
plus the contextual-tip eligibility). The model holds the analytics-endpoint shape verbatim (SI °C +
Wh/km); temperature (°C → °C/°F via the shared Units facade) and consumption (Wh/km → Wh/mi via the
inline km-per-mile factor, the web's KM_PER_MILE — there is no convertEfficiencyFromSI helper) convert
to the user's unit ONLY at the render boundary via TemperatureImpactFormat (ADR-005).

The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle + the global VehicleSelect) and ALL
8 of the manifest's panels:

  Panel 1 Avg-Efficiency      — TemperatureImpactSummarySection metric card (Panels.swift).
  Panel 2 Best-Temp-Range     — summary card; value = best band label, subtitle = mean Wh/km|Wh/mi.
  Panel 3 Worst-Temp-Range    — summary card; value = worst band label, subtitle = mean consumption.
  Panel 4 Total-Data-Points   — summary card; integer point count.
  Panel 5 (GlassPanel5)       — TemperatureImpactScatterSection: TSChartContainer hosting the native
                                Swift Charts TSScatterChart (Temperature vs Efficiency), one band-tinted
                                series per populated °C band (cold→hot), axis captions + band legend;
                                chart empty-overlay when there are no drives.
  Panel 6 (GlassPanel6)       — TemperatureImpactBucketSection: TSChartContainer hosting the native
                                Swift Charts TSLineChart (Efficiency by Temperature Range), one point per
                                band (display avg, 0 for empty bands), band-label axis + avg legend.
  Panel 7 (GlassPanel7)       — TemperatureImpactOptimalSection: optimal-temperature analysis (desc +
                                worst-vs-best savings delta + per-band badge row); common.noData
                                EmptyState (panel stays visible) when no band has data.
  Panel 8 (GlassPanel8)       — TemperatureImpactTipsSection: lightbulb-headed recommendations
                                (optimal-range / cold / hot tips), or the common.noData EmptyState.

Charts (2) — both native Swift Charts wrappers (P3), never a WKWebView: ScatterChart → TSScatterChart;
LineChart → TSLineChart.

States (4) — modeled by TemperatureImpactPhase: loading = .redacted skeleton (Chrome.swift); empty =
metric cards read "—" + both charts show their isEmpty overlay + optimal/tips show common.noData;
error = the web's non-blocking inline TSAlertBanner (error.loadFailed) above the still-rendered panels;
success = populated.

Adaptive (ADR-002/006): the header and the summary grid reflow 2-up (compact iPhone) / 4-up (macOS /
iPad regular) via the #if os(iOS) horizontalSizeClass guard (isCompact = false on macOS). All copy
resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (20 new bare keys added — common.noData and
error.loadFailed already present); a11y labels on panels + charts; Dynamic Type; light/dark via design
tokens (no hardcoded colors/typography; toned-down palette via TSChartPalette + Color.TS).

Navigation (mirrors the sibling unrouted RouteEfficiencyRouteRegistration; the .maps host is the
primary map overview, and /temperature-impact is not a dedicated enum case): typed
TemperatureImpactLink + .temperatureImpactDestination() NavigationDestination +
TemperatureImpactRouteRegistration.make() factory, with deep-link path "/temperature-impact" → .maps
added to AppRouteParser.aliases (like "/route-efficiency" → .driving).

Files (apps/apple/Sources/Features/Maps/):
  TemperatureImpactPageModel.swift          — @Observable model, types, phase, bucket math, data-source
  TemperatureImpactPageModel.Sample.swift   — Sample / Empty / Failing data sources
  TemperatureImpactFormat.swift             — display-boundary formatters (temp / efficiency / labels)
  TemperatureImpactPage.swift               — View + header + phase switch + previews
  TemperatureImpactPage.Panels.swift        — summary cards + optimal analysis + tips + flow layout
  TemperatureImpactPage.Charts.swift        — scatter ChartContainer + line ChartContainer
  TemperatureImpactPage.Chrome.swift        — loading skeleton
  TemperatureImpactRouteRegistration.swift  — typed-link NavigationDestination + factory
Tests (apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Maps/):
  TemperatureImpactPageModelTests.swift     — 12 state-machine/derivation tests
  TemperatureImpactFormatTests.swift        — 12 formatter tests
Edited: apps/apple/Sources/App/AppRouteParser.swift (alias),
        apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings (20 bare keys)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTES / DISCLOSURES (honesty covenant #1, #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- One genuine Swift-6 strict-concurrency fix was made to my own new code during the build loop and is
  disclosed here: the bucket-band constants (TemperatureImpactPageModel.bucketBoundsC / bucketIndex)
  are read by the nonisolated display layer (TemperatureImpactFormat default parameter), so they are
  marked `nonisolated` — they are pure domain constants, correctly main-actor-independent.
- The TeslaSyncTests bundle is large (~2,000 files / ~25k cases) and re-links the whole @testable app
  module, so the gate was scoped with -only-testing to THIS page's two test classes (24 cases). They
  build + run + pass; the rest of the suite was not exercised (out of scope, unchanged). The empty_count
  swiftlint rule and the lint scope match the sibling Features/Driving precedent.
- Pre-existing, OUT-OF-SCOPE, NOT masked: TeslaSync/feature-views/AnomalyInlineRow.Previews.swift:37,89
  carry two project-wide `swiftlint --strict` line_length violations (the same pair disclosed by the
  sibling RouteEfficiency log). They are outside the gate's Features/Maps lint scope and unrelated.

